198
00:14:21,719 --> 00:14:25,920
that he had just bought a hydroplane, and was going to try it out in the morning.

199
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:27,899
“Want to go with me, old sport?

200
00:14:27,899 --> 00:14:34,738
Just near the shore along the Sound.” “What time anytime that suits you best.”

201
00:14:34,738 --> 00:14:39,539
It was on the tip of my tongue to ask his name when Jordan looked around and smiled.

202
00:14:39,539 --> 00:14:45,479
“Having a gay time now?” she inquired. “Much better.” I turned again to my new acquaintance.

203
00:14:45,479 --> 00:14:51,359
“This is an unusual party for me. I haven’t even seen the host. I live over there—”

204
00:14:51,359 --> 00:14:55,859
