420
00:31:09,899 --> 00:31:14,279
Warwick, she left a borrowed car out in the rain with the top down, and then lied

421
00:31:14,279 --> 00:31:17,698
about it— —and suddenly I remembered the story about her that had eluded me that

422
00:31:17,698 --> 00:31:22,260
night at daisies At her first big golf tournament there was a row that nearly

423
00:31:22,260 --> 00:31:27,000
reached the newspapers— —a suggestion that she had moved her ball from a bad lie in

424
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:30,658
the semi-final round. The thing approached the proportions of a scandal—

425
00:31:30,658 --> 00:31:35,340
—then died away. A caddy retracted his statement, and the only other witness

426
00:31:35,340 --> 00:31:39,658
admitted that he might have been mistaken. The incident and the name had

427
00:31:39,658 --> 00:31:41,939
remained together in my mind.

428
00:31:41,939 --> 00:31:48,420
Jordan Baker instinctively avoided clever, shrewd men, and now I saw that this was because she

429
00:31:48,420 --> 00:31:53,698
felt safer on a plane where any Divergent from a code would be thought impossible.

430
00:31:53,698 --> 00:31:59,698
She was incurably dishonest. She wasn’t able to endure being at a disadvantage

431
00:31:59,698 --> 00:32:04,319
and, given this unwillingness, I suppose she had begun dealing in subterfuges

432
00:32:04,319 --> 00:32:10,560
when she was very young in order to keep that cool, insolent smile turned to the world

433
00:32:10,560 --> 00:32:15,479
and yet satisfy the demands of her hard, jaunty body.

434
00:32:15,479 --> 00:32:20,939
It made no difference to me. Dishonesty in a woman is a thing you never blame deeply—

435
00:32:20,939 --> 00:32:24,658
—I was casually sorry, and then I forgot.

436
00:32:24,658 --> 00:32:30,060
It was on that same house party that we had a curious conversation about driving a car.

437
00:32:30,060 --> 00:32:34,439
It started because she passed so close to some workmen that our fender flicked

438
00:32:34,439 --> 00:32:36,899
a button on one man’s coat.

439
00:32:36,899 --> 00:32:39,899
“You’re a rotten driver,” I protested.

440
00:32:39,899 --> 00:32:45,960
“Either you ought to be more careful were you ought to drive at all.” “I am careful.”

441
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:51,719
“No, you’re not.” “Well, other people are,” she said lightly.

442
00:32:51,719 --> 00:32:57,779
“What’s that got to do with it?” “They’ll keep out of my way,” she insisted.

443
00:32:57,779 --> 00:33:04,079
“It takes two to make an accident.” “Suppose you met somebody just as careless as yourself.”

444
00:33:04,079 --> 00:33:07,619
“I hope I never will,” she answered.

445
00:33:07,619 --> 00:33:10,319
“I hate careless people.

446
00:33:10,319 --> 00:33:16,380
That’s why I like you.” Her gray Sun's strained eyes stared straight ahead,

447
00:33:16,380 --> 00:33:22,859
but she had deliberately shifted our relations, and for a moment I thought I loved her.

448
00:33:22,859 --> 00:33:29,279
But I'm slow thinking and full of interior rules that act as breaks on my desires,

449
00:33:29,279 --> 00:33:35,158
and I knew that first I had to get myself definitely out of that tangle back home

450
00:33:35,158 --> 00:33:39,539
I've been writing letters once a week and signing them: “Love neck and all I

451
00:33:39,539 --> 00:33:45,300
could think of was how, when that certain girl played tennis, a faint mustache of perspiration

452
00:33:45,300 --> 00:33:47,520
appeared on her upper lip.

453
00:33:47,520 --> 00:33:51,658
Nevertheless there was a vague understanding that had to be tactfully

454
00:33:51,658 --> 00:33:54,359
broken off before I was free.

455
00:33:54,359 --> 00:34:00,960
Everyone suspects himself of at least one of the cardinal virtues, and this is mine:

456
00:34:00,960 --> 00:34:06,000
I am one of the few honest people that I have ever known
